+For enumeration, create a second distinct external seal with `mode=enumerate`, a new run ID, `binary` copied exactly from the reviewed build receipt's `binary_candidate`, and `build_receipt` pinned by real path/size/SHA. Keep the same reviewed package and original dependency pins. Then use the same command shape with enumeration mode and that second seal. No placeholders are executable instructions for this worker; no command above was executed.
+
+Child enumeration environment is built from scratch: `PATH=/usr/bin:/bin`, `HOME=/home/yayoi`, `LANG=C.UTF-8`, `LC_ALL=C.UTF-8`, `PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1`, `ZET_ENABLE_METRICS=1`, `NEOReadDebugKeys=1`, `EnableDirectSubmission=0`. No inherited `LD_PRELOAD`, tracing collector, `SYCL_*`, `UR_*`, `UNITRACE_*`, `XPTI_*`, `ZE_AFFINITY_MASK` or selector is enrolled. This isolates the raw Level Zero enumeration question. Every control is fixed in the native child's environment before exec. API entry/results are self-traced by the helper; no collection/tracing layer is injected. Compile uses its separately recorded immutable host environment and LLVM library directory only.
+
+The existing `owned-v0141-measurement.lock` is acquired nonblocking. Main is responsible for serializing foreign GPU/build/test/cleanup work; this source does not inspect or signal foreign processes. Build whole budget is 240 seconds, child wall 120/CPU 90 seconds; enumeration whole budget 120, child wall 60/CPU 30 seconds. Each owned session has 2 GiB RSS, 32 MiB raw text/file and 128 MiB private-artifact caps; 40 seconds are reserved for closure. `direct_owner.py` adds its existing finite pidfd/session/process-count limits. A budget stop remains incomplete.
